# NOTE: .env* files are intentionally NOT excluded here. sessionops/settings.py
# requires a physical .env.{ENVIRONMENT} file to exist inside the container at
# runtime (BASE_DIR / f".env.{ENVIRONMENT}") — it's not just relying on
# docker-compose's `env_file:` process-env injection, it re-reads the file from
# disk itself. Excluding .env.* here breaks every deployment (confirmed: staging
# failed to boot with "Env file not found: /app/.env.staging" after this was
# tried). The correct fix for "don't bake secrets into random dev environments'
# images" is per-developer discipline (don't build from a directory with .env
# files you don't want in that image) or a settings.py change to accept
# injected env vars without requiring the physical file — not a blanket
# .dockerignore exclusion, since this app's config loader genuinely needs it.

# Version control / IDE
.git
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Local data / logs — not needed in the image, may contain sensitive output
sessionops/logs/*.log*
db.sqlite3
secrets/
data/
